CFM will determine which parts are required to perform the Services and will provide all parts and materials (new, used Serviceable, or Rotable Parts). Title to parts and material furnished by CFM will pass to Customer upon incorporation in the Engine.

{CFM shall obtain written approval from Customer before installing any used Serviceable Parts on the Engine. For avoidance of doubt, Customer shall respond to CFM with a decision of approval or refusal within [days_for_answer] Day, any extra time spent on Customer communication per this paragraph should be added to the TAT.}

Customer shall retain title to removed Parts and such removed Parts shall be held at the DRS for [days] Days for the Customer to review and/or retrieve them. After such period, any Parts not retrieved by Customer become CFM property {[return]}.

{CFM shall inform Customer for the disposition of such removed Parts no later than [CFM_days_to_inform] Days before the end of the Period. After such Period, any Parts not retrieved by Customer become CFM property.}

CFM may elect to use parts from its Rotable Parts inventory to replace Customer’s repairable parts, which will be repaired by CFM at Customer’s expense. If such removed parts are later scrapped, condemned or determined to be non-repairable, or under limitation (such as, but not limited to a Customer Departure Record), Customer will pay for the replacement part as detailed in the widget "FPLS Grid", less any applicable exchange fee previously paid and the parts will be disposed of at no expense to Customer. 

Title to Rotable Parts furnished by CFM will pass to Customer upon incorporation in the Engine, and simultaneously, title to the parts replaced will pass to CFM.

Rotable Parts shall not be used to replace a Part coming from an Engine that has been subject to an accident or misuse.

{Prior to use Ratable Parts from its Ratable Parts inventory, CFM will request Customer's prior approval to be received by CFM within [days_from_request] Days from request. In case Customer fail to give its approval within [days_for_approval] Days, the guaranteed TAT will be extended accordingly.}

{Customer agrees to delegate approval to use Rotable Parts to CFM for non-LLP parts if the Rotable Part meets the following cumulative criteria : [criteria]}

{If Customer is unwilling to accept the use of Rotable Parts, or desires to provide his own parts, TAT target may have to be readjusted. In any case, parts from Customer’s own fleet or Customer Furnished Equipment shall be provided within [days] days after the Engine disassembly is completed, otherwise Rotable Parts will be provided.}

Upon Delivery, CFM will notify Customer of any components or [missing_items] missing from the Engine. CFM will replace such missing items at Customer’s expense as Supplemental Services, unless:
- CFM notifies Customer in writing within [hours_days] [unit] after receiving CFM’s notice that Customer wishes to furnish such missing items;-
- Customer delivers such missing items to the CFM Designated Repair Station within [weeks] weeks.  

{In order to complete the test cell run, in the event any component or Engine Controls and Accessories item is missing from the Engine, CFM may, at Customer’s request, fit its own item if available. This loan service is applicable to components or Engine Controls and Accessories with a current supplier spare parts catalog list price value lower than [value] [currency].}

{In such a case, five [days] Days shall be added to the TAT for the relevant Engine. This slave item shall be removed from the Engine before the Engine shipment.}

{For such loan service, Customer will be charged an amount of [amount] [currency] per missing item and per test cell run. CFM may, at CFM’s sole discretion, provide such loan service to items with higher value, which will be charged at [percent] percent of the current item supplier spare parts price catalog.}

{For [engine-parts] repaired and Redelivered within [months-before-expiration] calendar months preceding expiration of its [period] [contract]}
If Customer claims a defect in workmanship within {either [months-of-operation] calendar months of operation or}
[months-following-redelivery] calendar months following Redelivery, or [EFH-numbers] EFH, whichever comes first and
{Customer provides written notice to CFM of such defect within thirty [days-of-discovery] Days of its discovery}, and
{Customer ships to CFM the part or component which gives rise to the claim to the facility directed by CFM within [days] days, or, in cases in which shipment is commercially impracticable, makes such part or component reasonably available to CFM’s personnel} and

{CFM reasonably establishes that Customer’s claim is correct, CFM will provide or cause to provide, at CFM’S option, [following]: [CFM-warranty-options].}

{If any QEC or accessory had been repaired during shop visit and found fault within [EFH] EFH after installation and subject to CFM's defective performance, CFM shall pay a penalty of [penalty] [currency] per occurence.}
